jruby(1) -- Interpreted object-oriented scripting language
==========================================================

## SYNOPSIS

`<%= synopsis %>`

## DESCRIPTION

JRuby is a pure-Java implementation of the Ruby programming language.
It is an interpreted scripting language for quick and easy
object-oriented programming, with many features for processing text files
and for system management tasks.
The command-line switches accepted by the interpreter are described below;
they are largely similar to those of `ruby(1)` and `perl(1)`.

## OPTIONS

The switches are also listed in abbreviated form by `jruby --help`.

<% options.each do |option| -%>
`<%= option.flag %>`
: <%= option.description %>

<% end -%>
## ENVIRONMENT

`JRUBY_OPTS`
: Additional command-line options prepended to the ones given on the command line.

`JRUBY_HOME`
: The directory of the JRuby installation.

